    description: "One hundred and forty-three pāsurams of longing, dream, and devotional passion — Āṇṭāḷ's second and greater work, in which she speaks as a woman consumed by love for Tirumāl, sending messengers, interpreting omens, weeping for the absent Lord, and finally surrendering in total union.",
    context: "Where the Thiruppāvai is a communal dawn-vigil, the Nācciyār Tirumoḻi is intensely personal — a single voice burning with separation (viraha) and longing for the divine beloved. It stands as one of the greatest love poems in Tamil literature."
  },

  decads: [
    { num: 1,  tamil: "தையொரு திங்களும்",     english: "The Month of Thai",            verses: "1–10",   count: 10, theme: "The vow of Kāma-deva — Āṇṭāḷ observes the Kāma-nōmbu (love-rite) vowing to offer ritual worship so that she may win Tirumāl as her husband." },
    { num: 2,  tamil: "நாமவன் நாரணன்",        english: "His Name is Nārāyaṇa",         verses: "11–20",  count: 10, theme: "The dream — Āṇṭāḷ describes seeing Tirumāl in a dream and the overwhelming joy that follows." },
    { num: 3,  tamil: "வாரணமாயிரம்",           english: "A Thousand Elephants",         verses: "21–30",  count: 10, theme: "The wedding dream — Āṇṭāḷ dreams of her marriage to Tirumāl and describes the procession of a thousand elephants." },
    { num: 4,  tamil: "வேண்டு நன்குடையீர்",   english: "You Who Have Fine Desires",    verses: "31–40",  count: 10, theme: "Sending messengers — Āṇṭāḷ calls on birds and clouds to carry her longing to the Lord." },
    { num: 5,  tamil: "எந்தை தந்தை",           english: "My Father's Father",           verses: "41–50",  count: 10, theme: "Ancestral devotion — she traces her lineage of devotion back through generations." },
    { num: 6,  tamil: "வாழ் திருமாலே",          english: "Long Live Tirumāl",           verses: "51–60",  count: 10, theme: "The kuyil messenger — Āṇṭāḷ sends the koel bird as her messenger to the absent Lord." },
    { num: 7,  tamil: "கிளியினம் கூட்டம்",     english: "The Flock of Parrots",        verses: "61–70",  count: 10, theme: "The parrot messenger — she addresses a flock of parrots, teaching them to speak her Lord's name." },
    { num: 8,  tamil: "விலாவிய கோல்",          english: "The Curving Branch",          verses: "71–80",  count: 10, theme: "Separation and nature imagery — clouds, rivers, and trees are all addressed as witnesses to her longing." },
    { num: 9,  tamil: "சிற்றில் சிறுமாடு",    english: "The Little House",            verses: "81–90",  count: 10, theme: "Childhood play — Āṇṭāḷ recalls building little houses of sand with her friends, a metaphor for the soul's play in the world." },
    { num: 10, tamil: "கொண்டல் கொண்ட",         english: "The Cloud That Holds",        verses: "91–100", count: 10, theme: "The cloud messenger — she sends the monsoon cloud to carry her message to Tirumāl." },
    { num: 11, tamil: "நொந்தாமரை",             english: "The Unwithered Lotus",        verses: "101–110",count: 10, theme: "Signs and omens — Āṇṭāḷ interprets natural phenomena as signs of the Lord's presence or absence." },
    { num: 12, tamil: "ஒரு திங்கள்",            english: "A Single Month",              verses: "111–120",count: 10, theme: "The fever of separation — she has been apart from the Lord for a month; her suffering is described in the language of love-sickness." },
